----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 CHANGES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-----------------
Version 1.2->1.3:
-----------------
-  "LowMemory" tooltype may be set to permanently engage Low-Memory mode.
(ie, a 10K memory buffer and incremental directory reading).  PLEASE read
the section describing this option. 

-  A  Nuke  program  may  be  called from within FR, using the "X" command
during listing pause.  The nuker name may be set with the "Nuker" tooltype
and access required may be set with the "NukeAccess" tooltype.

-  A  file  numbering system has been integrated.  Files may be flagged by
their  filename as well as by their number.  To adopt this as default, set
the  "FileNumbers"  tooltype to YES.  The user may turn this option on/off
with  config  option  7.    (The  side  effects of using file numbers: the
file-check byte will not be shown in the listing, and the year will be cut
off from the date.)

-  I  have taken  the popular registration approach.  How do you register? 
Well,  disableds are nice.  Personal Checks are GREAT.  Source code to ACP
3.XX  is  spectacular.  Calling cards are keen.  A nocTurne deSign logo is
fucking EXCELLENT.  Or you can tear out the old hex editor, I suppose. 

- I made a GUIDE, dammit.  Why aren't you READING it??

-----------------
Version 1.1->1.2:
-----------------
-  Incremental  directory  reading is now available.  Versions prior to this
one  required  an amount of memory equal to the size of the file listings to
be  available.    Now,  if  that  memory  is  unavailable, FR will engage in
low-memory  mode,  and use a buffer of 10K.  Of course the program will slow
down  a  bit  for  intermittant  disk accessing.  DATE-SCANS ARE DISABLED in
Low-Memory Mode.  (Does anybody USE them anyway??)

-  All  information  is now stored in the drawer 'noC-FR' which should be in
'DOORS:'.

-  Bug-Fixes:  Last entry in a file listing is now displayed,  nuke messages
are now  handled properly,  file-flag  field may now be cleared with CTRL-X,
and other internal changes...

-----------------
Version 1.0->1.1:
-----------------
-  File-flagging  has  a new look, and no longer shifts the list up when you
hit enter.

-  Now no longer PAUSES 2 TIMES with newer /X versions.

-  Other various design changes and bug-fixes.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 FINAL NOTES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Please  note that I have not plugged any BBS's in this program, nor will I
 in  any  future doors.  The code has been bug-tested on multi-node systems
 of  varying  configurations  and  has  no known backdoors.  Support may be
 obtained by calling Sarcophagus (+1.503.548.0532), or leaving me a message
 on  a  board  you see me on.  Therefore I see no reason NOT to use FR.  It
 should prove to be a great asset to the users of your board.

